---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
import { breadcrumbNode } from '../lib/schema';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Who builds AI Blog Writer with Sources, why it is source-first, and how to get in touch."
  schema={[
    breadcrumbNode([{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'About', path: '/about/' }]),
    { '@type': 'AboutPage', url: `${SITE.url}/about/`, mainEntity: { '@id': `${SITE.url}/about/#person` } },
  ]}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>Built by Luis Rita</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        {SITE.productName} is an independent WordPress plugin designed, built and supported by {SITE.author.name}.
      </p>

      <h2>Why source-first</h2>
      <p>
        Generating a draft has become easy. It's now built into editors, hosts and SEO plugins. What's still hard is
        publishing AI-assisted content you can defend: knowing where each claim came from, spotting what went stale, and
        keeping a consistent voice. This plugin is built around that problem. It writes from sources you choose, cites
        them, and stops at a draft so a person decides what goes live.
      </p>

      <h2>Principles</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Drafts, never auto-publish.</strong> A person stays responsible for what's published.</li>
        <li><strong>Your data stays yours.</strong> Your key, your provider, your database. Nothing is sent to the author.</li>
        <li><strong>Plain about limits.</strong> No ranking, traffic or accuracy guarantees.</li>
        <li><strong>WordPress-native.</strong> Core blocks, real author accounts and standard privacy tools.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Support, bug reports, security issues and partnership questions:
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>. For bugs, attach the JSON report from
        <strong>AI Blog Writer → Diagnostics</strong>. It leaves out keys and content.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
